{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrangeThemeSelectInputComponentTokensProvider","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    \/\/ Define your own provider for select input component tokens","    \/\/ by inheriting from existing provider","    class CustomSelectInputComponentTokensProvider: OrangeThemeSelectInputComponentTokensProvider {","","        \/\/ Then override the select input component tokens you want.","","        override var selectSizeMaxHeightContainerIcon: SizeSemanticToken { DimensionRawTokens._600 }","","        \/\/ ...","    }","","    \/\/ Or define your own provider from scratch","    class CustomSelectInoutComponentTokensProvider: SelectInputComponentTokens {","","        \/\/ And implement hunders of tokens.","        \/\/ You are allowed to give semantic tokens providers if you want to define values.","    }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Then, you can give this ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomSelectInputComponentTokensProvider","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to your own theme implementation:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["class LocalTheme: OrangeTheme {","","    override init() {","        super.init(selectInput: CustomSelectInputComponentTokensProvider())","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"or to an already existing theme for example:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    OrangeTheme(selectInput: CustomSelectInputComponentTokensProvider())"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is also possible to use your own semantic tokens providers for this component tokens providers:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    \/\/ Uses by default